  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 'Log - [unassigned 1]'
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: 'Log - [unassigned 1]'
  logTitle: Routine Maintenance
  author: '[Captain TBD]'
  shipName: '[Unassigned]'
  dateRecorded: '[TBD]'
  logText: 'Spent most of the morning trying to get the ventilation fan in the aft
    compartment working properly again.

    It''s been making a rattling noise
    for the better part of a week. Nothing serious, but there''s only so much of
    that I can listen to before it starts getting on my nerves.

    Turns out one
    of the mounting brackets had worked itself loose. Tightened it, checked the others,
    and gave the whole assembly a good cleaning while I was at it.

    The noise
    is gone now.

    I''ve also noticed the water reclamation system is running
    a little less efficiently than it should. Probably just needs another filter
    change. I''ll put that on tomorrow''s list.

    Otherwise, everything''s holding
    together.

    Not exactly exciting work, but I suppose that''s a good thing.
    Out here, boring is usually preferable.'
